// Stands in for the thing that costs money: one execution of this workflow = one side effect.
// responseMode is onReceived on purpose. The caller (the gate's "Do the work" node) must not have to
// wait for a worker slot to free up: with WORKER_CONCURRENCY x workers slots all taken by a burst of
// gate executions, a gate execution waiting for THIS one to finish would wait for a slot that only it
// could release.
return [{ json: { did: $input.first().json.body, exec: $execution.id } }];
